ions":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntervalTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Stein, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Introduction to Algorithms"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with different values.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var meetings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","meetings.insert(9 ..< 10, value: \"stand-up\")","meetings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"design review\")","meetings.insert(11 ..< 13, value: \"lunch\")","meetings.containing(11).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"design review\", \"lunch\"]","meetings.overlapping(9 ..< 11).map(\\.value)   \/\/ [\"stand-up\", \"design review\"]","meetings.contained(in: 9 ..< 12).map(\\.range) \/\/ [9 ..< 10, 10 ..< 12]"]},{